---
import FeaturesLayout from '../../layouts/FeaturesLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const howToJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: 'Gate a CI build on documentation coverage',
  description:
    'Use compodocx --coverageMinimum to make CI fail when public-symbol documentation drops below your threshold.',
  totalTime: 'PT5M',
  tool: [{ '@type': 'HowToTool', name: '@cngxjs/compodocx' }],
  step: [
    {
      '@type': 'HowToStep',
      position: 1,
      name: 'Pick a starting threshold',
      text: 'Most projects start at 50% and ratchet up. Set whatever number reflects the strictness you can defend on every PR.',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'HowToStep',
      position: 2,
      name: 'Run compodocx with --coverageMinimum',
      text: 'Add --coverageMinimum 80 to the docs build command in your CI pipeline. Anything below 80% public-symbol documentation will exit non-zero.',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'HowToStep',
      position: 3,
      name: 'Optionally scope to public API only',
      text: 'Pass --publicApiOnly to compute coverage against the exported allow-list, so internal helpers do not drag the percentage down.',
    },
  ],
};
---

<FeaturesLayout
  currentSlug="coverage"
  title="Documentation Coverage — CI gating in compodocx"
  description="Per-symbol compodocx documentation coverage with CI threshold gating via --coverageMinimum. coverage.json with schemaVersion for dashboard ingestion."
  extraJsonLd={howToJsonLd}
>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary text-lg">
    Every run produces a coverage report. The percentage of public symbols carrying at least a
    one-line description. Below the threshold, the CLI exits non-zero so CI can gate.
  </p>

  <h2>Gating in CI</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="npx compodocx -p tsconfig.doc.json --coverageMinimum 80" />
  <p>
    Anything below 80% in the example above fails the build. Set the threshold based on the
    strictness you&rsquo;re aiming for. Most projects start at 50% and move it up as gaps close.
  </p>

  <h2>What counts as documented</h2>
  <p>
    A public symbol counts as documented when its JSDoc block has a non-empty description on the
    first line. Tags alone (<code class="cdx-code">@param</code>,
    <code class="cdx-code">@returns</code>) do not satisfy the description requirement; they augment
    it. Members marked <code class="cdx-code">@internal</code> are excluded entirely.
  </p>

  <h2>Coverage tab</h2>
  <p>
    The HTML output renders a <em>Documentation Coverage</em> tab on the project root: the overall percentage,
    breakdown by entity kind (components, directives, classes, interfaces, etc.), and a sortable list
    of undocumented symbols with deep links to their source.
  </p>

  <h2>Public-API filtering</h2>
  <p>
    When <code class="cdx-code">--publicApiOnly</code> is set, coverage is computed against the allow-list.
    Internal symbols stop dragging the percentage down, and the report focuses on the surface consumers
    actually see.
  </p>
</FeaturesLayout>
